---
---
<section class="card hidden" data-step="sort-group">
  <div class="pill mb-3">Step 4: Group ranking</div>
  <h3 class="text-xl font-display">Rank this group of titles</h3>
  <p class="text-sm text-latte-subtext1">
    Drag the titles into order. This order gives the model a better signal
    than one comparison.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-latte-subtext0">
    Keyboard: focus a title. Then use the Arrow keys to move between titles.
    Use Alt+Arrow (or Ctrl+Arrow) to move the title up or down.
  </p>
  <ul
    class="sortable-list"
    data-sortable-list
    role="listbox"
    aria-label="Titles to rank, best first"
    aria-orientation="vertical"
  ></ul>
  <p class="visually-hidden" data-sort-group-live aria-live="polite"></p>
  <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-latte-subtext0" data-group-coverage>
    Coverage: 0 / 0 titles compared (0 not compared)
  </p>
  <p class="text-xs text-latte-subtext0" data-group-estimate>
    Baseline target: ~0 group sorts (~2 sorts per title).
  </p>
  <p class="text-xs text-latte-subtext0">
    You can stop early. If you do fewer group sorts, the ranking is less
    accurate. For more stability, run the uncertainty analysis or use
    pairwise refine.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <button class="btn" type="button" data-action="submit-sort">
      Submit ranking
    </button>
    <button class="btn-secondary" type="button" data-action="skip-sort">
      Skip this group sort
    </button>
    <button
      class="btn-secondary hidden"
      type="button"
      data-action="switch-to-pairwise"
    >
      Switch to pairwise refine
    </button>
  </div>
</section>
